IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`
IMPORT `ita-rules`

-- Income Tax Act 2007 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Seat: the individual
-- taxpayer.
--
--   "What is my personal allowance this year? How much income tax do I owe
--    on my wages, savings and dividends? Can I transfer part of my allowance
--    to my spouse or civil partner, and what is it worth if I receive it?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Taxpayer position` HAS
    `adjusted net income`                               IS A NUMBER
    `personal allowance`                                IS A NUMBER
    `savings allowance`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `tax before reductions`                             IS A NUMBER
    `marriage allowance reduction`                      IS A NUMBER
    `income tax liability`                              IS A NUMBER
    `I may elect to transfer my allowance`              IS A BOOLEAN

@ref ss 10-16, 23, 35, 55B-55C, 58, 414-415
@export default The individual taxpayer's position under the Income Tax Act 2007 (UK), for a UK resident who is not a Scottish or Welsh taxpayer and has no property income: adjusted net income (s 58), personal allowance with the £100,000 taper (s 35), savings allowance (s 12B), tax before reductions on non-savings, savings and dividend income through the bands as extended by Gift Aid and pension contributions (ss 10-16, 414), the marriage allowance reduction (s 55B), the income tax liability, and whether I may elect to transfer part of my allowance (s 55C). The basic, higher and additional rates and the savings rates are inputs, as set by Parliament for the year. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Taxpayer`  @desc The rates for the year, my income, Gift Aid, pension contributions and marriage allowance position
GIVETH A `Taxpayer position`
`the taxpayer position for` t MEANS
    `Taxpayer position` WITH
        `adjusted net income`                           IS `my adjusted net income` t
        `personal allowance`                            IS `my personal allowance` t
        `savings allowance`                             IS `my savings allowance` t
        `tax before reductions`                         IS `my tax before reductions` t
        `marriage allowance reduction`                  IS `my marriage allowance reduction` t
        `income tax liability`                          IS `my income tax liability` t
        `I may elect to transfer my allowance`          IS `I may elect to transfer my allowance` t
